# Vendored third-party libraries (JSZip, Tesseract.js + its worker + WASM
# core) must be treated as binary — never line-ending-normalized by Git. Their
# exact byte counts are validated against upstream (see docs/superpowers
# review notes for the OCR/CSP fix), and this box's own git config has
# core.autocrlf=true at the system level, which would otherwise silently
# rewrite LF -> CRLF on every future checkout and drift the vendored files
# away from their audited bytes.
web/*.min.js -text
pwa/*.min.js -text
web/*.wasm.js -text
pwa/*.wasm.js -text
